{"version":3,"kind":"Notebook","sha256":"98183443699060a30d2388003e2d98e9a206dac684669f8cb84fec0f9dd9113e","slug":"crocodash.projects.ocean-only","location":"/crocodash/projects/ocean_only.ipynb","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"Project: Ocean Only Configuration - The Bare Minimum","content_includes_title":false,"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"CrocoDash","language":"python"},"github":"https://github.com/CROCODILE-CESM/CrocoGallery","numbering":{"title":{"offset":2}},"source_url":"https://github.com/CROCODILE-CESM/CrocoGallery/blob/main/crocodash/projects/ocean_only.ipynb","edit_url":"https://github.com/CROCODILE-CESM/CrocoGallery/edit/main/crocodash/projects/ocean_only.ipynb","exports":[{"format":"ipynb","filename":"ocean_only.ipynb","url":"/CrocoGallery/latest/build/ocean_only-a0d4c2d45278b432b4afc897cd547617.ipynb"}]},"widgets":{},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This project is all about how we create the most basic ocean_only domain to shake things out and get spinning as fast as possible. This is one way of testing everything before we get into our research questions.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"Qwrp5XQKGn"}],"key":"ChdHE7UmE3"}],"identifier":"84b4b4ad","html_id":"84b4b4ad","key":"iyApopZDzF"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Download this project by either:","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"rWEoPYZxOS"}],"key":"c9SYA6x789"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Running the CrocoDash CLI command: ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"ov37SdaLJJ"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"crocodash template --output ocean_only_case.ipynb --machine glade --notebook crocodash.projects.ocean_only","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"NjTNK2ODvR"},{"type":"text","value":", then filling in the paths it leaves as placeholders","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"eXzZSd6LSL"}],"key":"PwErGOCyuf"}],"key":"lMw3I0rJiJ"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Copying the file from your CrocoDash checkout: ","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"kkGOk34rHK"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gallery/crocodash/projects/ocean_only.ipynb","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"yszcG3AR6G"}],"key":"yJlXvwdX8u"}],"key":"iN2Nd70BJy"}],"key":"P7HjmBOenI"}],"identifier":"d75d080e","html_id":"d75d080e","key":"RHbzTYGSe9"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grid Generation","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"nJnvvvVok8"}],"identifier":"grid-generation","label":"Grid Generation","html_id":"grid-generation","implicit":true,"key":"n74ZCxJRO9"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The first thing we are going to do is think about how to get a domain. Scaling data is available online, but a 100x100 point domain is relatively quick. If we provide ~40 cores for the ocean, it’ll run within a few minutes.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"SpuBe3DrIs"}],"key":"UzE8zgv6Fv"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"We’ll pick a 100x100 point horizontal grid and a standard vertical grid.","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"bf4N6bbQSM"}],"key":"TbcRfoFfhV"}],"identifier":"e0fc8055","html_id":"e0fc8055","key":"uoLHxTVIHP"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"from CrocoDash.grid import Grid\nfrom CrocoDash.vgrid import VGrid\n\ngrid = Grid(\n  resolution = 0.05, # in degrees\n  xstart = 278.0, # min longitude in [0, 360]\n  lenx = 5.0, # longitude extent in degrees\n  ystart = 7.0, # min latitude in [-90, 90]\n  leny = 5.0, # latitude extent in degrees\n  name = \"basic_grid\",\n)\n\n\nvgrid  = VGrid.hyperbolic(\n    nk = 75, # number of vertical levels\n    depth = 2000,\n    ratio=20.0 # target ratio of top to bottom layer thicknesses\n)","key":"BWgWuYiOfX"},{"type":"outputs","id":"A6NPAbF9FTsHcT-4Tu1iC","children":[],"key":"TAEQgTYvg5"}],"identifier":"0325b73d","html_id":"0325b73d","key":"QwIe63lVL0"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Now that we have our horizontal and vertical grids, we need to setup our bathymetry. Normally, we’d use the ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"b2ndeWf7tf"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Topo.set_from_dataset","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"Mxpcvqrwbu"},{"type":"text","value":" function to go from a bathymetry dataset to grid bathymetry. However, as a first step we’ll skip the dataset entirely and use an idealized bathymetry. ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"mLzMhR9nfu"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Topo","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"o5roF5vtSP"},{"type":"text","value":" provides helpers mirroring MOM6’s built-in TOPO_CONFIG options, such as ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"BOuUNGZa1g"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"spoon","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"CnNXf800BA"},{"type":"text","value":", the analytic basin shape used in MOM6’s idealized double gyre case.","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"Fv3uQDYnyq"}],"key":"cjFC2Kw9xA"}],"identifier":"35338f50","html_id":"35338f50","key":"Qlox6ijkcd"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"from CrocoDash.topo import Topo\n\ntopo = Topo(\n    grid = grid,\n    min_depth = 9.5, # in meters\n)\n\ntopo.set_spoon(max_depth = 2000, dedge = 200)\n\ntopo.depth.plot()","key":"ZCC9656SzD"},{"type":"outputs","id":"KD8Bs__VOUyAsZYhN498_","children":[],"key":"OVFTAiIf32"}],"identifier":"664779d2","html_id":"664779d2","key":"zJwKopG7sE"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Great! So I’m going to create my case now, and this step will hardly ever change!","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"yU25Dyo8R7"}],"key":"DvGTKX9ULg"}],"identifier":"4e386f52","html_id":"4e386f52","key":"qzwejVToPK"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"from pathlib import Path\nfrom CrocoDash.case import Case\n\n# CESM case (experiment) name\ncasename = \"basic_ocean\"\n\n# CESM source root (Update this path accordingly!!!)\ncesmroot =\"<CESM>\"\n\n# Place where all your input files go \ninputdir = Path(\"<inputdir>\") / casename\n    \n# CESM case directory\ncaseroot = Path(\"<casedir>\") / casename\n\n\ncase = Case(\n    cesmroot = cesmroot,\n    caseroot = caseroot,\n    inputdir = inputdir,\n    ocn_grid = grid,\n    ocn_vgrid = vgrid,\n    ocn_topo = topo,\n    project = \"<PROJECT>\", # Update this with your project code\n    job_queue = \"<JOB_QUEUE>\", # PBS queue the run is submitted to\n    job_wallclock_time = \"<WALLCLOCK_1H>\", # hh:mm:ss walltime requested for the run\n    override = True,\n    machine = \"derecho\",\n    compset = \"CR_JRA\"\n)","key":"kaWJFKB4II"},{"type":"outputs","id":"Vuf_CE7uHaVtsh3pAEoJV","children":[],"key":"GQnDyACeBJ"}],"identifier":"ca45d4f1","html_id":"ca45d4f1","key":"i3xpmlwYhu"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Now, the last step is to generate forcings, which is done as a two step configure and process. Since it can take a long time to get raw data from outside sources, we’re going to use a fake data generator that comes with CrocoDash.","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"cfKpYLHoIy"}],"key":"o9eYifiD1c"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I also think we can run for 60 days. That doesn’t sound too bad.","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"OkIDAP3njH"}],"key":"cTzHP0gbE7"}],"identifier":"44b97111","html_id":"44b97111","key":"to6ytJegfY"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"case.configure_forcings(\n    date_range = [\"2019-01-01 00:00:00\", \"2019-03-03 00:00:00\"],\n    product_name=\"reference_ocean\",\n    function_name=\"get_reference_ocean_data\"\n)\n","key":"dpOS1gzK3R"},{"type":"outputs","id":"HaFI5aohyv7PMIvVurXLE","children":[],"key":"oJQ4rOZcf0"}],"identifier":"7ff41626","html_id":"7ff41626","key":"rSjr7ztUzz"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"case.process_forcings()\n","key":"fopsVlE7jO"},{"type":"outputs","id":"DeXR5TLc5MjywXRfDRVtH","children":[],"key":"rQ7fsu5rt4"}],"identifier":"890857d3","html_id":"890857d3","key":"M4gOfnIupf"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-content","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cool! Once this is done, we have to ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"bi7Go1hZRG"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"./case.build","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"PS0XFGYzyg"},{"type":"text","value":" and ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"H8bXZ8uQ7t"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"./case.submit","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"MFLXcGhD1q"},{"type":"text","value":" in our case directory. Before that though, here’s some things I’d ","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"ZshmNj53CE"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xmlchange","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"pHaz3xQyik"},{"type":"text","value":" to make the domain run faster.","position":{"start":{"line":1,"column":1},"end":{"line":1,"column":1}},"key":"qaTLbdP6wC"}],"key":"Hf4aP0I9Sl"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":8,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I’d set the ","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"qxgfy5mQK3"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NTASKS = 10","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"e2yBKrLq4k"},{"type":"text","value":", which sets every component to 10 cores, and makes the data atmosphere regridding very fast. (All components share these 10 cores)","position":{"start":{"line":3,"column":1},"end":{"line":3,"column":1}},"key":"fugZxq1jb5"}],"key":"dQaiiNTxkT"}],"key":"RUq8Zt0Ct7"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I’d set the ","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"cfLMU10mfL"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NTASKS_OCN = 40","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"VdXkhRW8w0"},{"type":"text","value":" because of the scaling data we saw: ","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"H460exJRHC"},{"type":"link","url":"https://crocodile-cesm.github.io/SeaSloth/mom6_scaling.html","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"https://​crocodile​-cesm​.github​.io​/SeaSloth​/mom6​_scaling​.html","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"TPW9IajbZQ"}],"urlSource":"https://crocodile-cesm.github.io/SeaSloth/mom6_scaling.html","key":"O0Cp8OMnBH"}],"key":"fEn96ICXeC"}],"key":"q4ubze4tO5"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I’d set the ","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"fzBLEbvTiN"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ROOTPE = 0","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"LIIZIJvJDo"},{"type":"text","value":", which ensures that all components share the same cores. If I set ROOTPE_OCN=10, it would skip the first 10 cores and run on the next 40 cores.","position":{"start":{"line":5,"column":1},"end":{"line":5,"column":1}},"key":"WyymnqGQ9e"}],"key":"Sm7yKnBgMh"}],"key":"qzWHsctQ7H"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":8,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I’d set the ","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"xqCkEtS1IJ"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"JOB_WALLCLOCK_TIME = 00:30:00 --subgroup case.run","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"JW42k2KVLa"},{"type":"text","value":", which ensures the queue picks up our job realllly fast.","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"h4C4z5qeQi"}],"key":"YA1S8OZ2jL"}],"key":"yaS6E9ghEb"}],"key":"ObunAKbqZn"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"And there we go! A fake running ocean model! Isn’t that awesome!","position":{"start":{"line":9,"column":1},"end":{"line":9,"column":1}},"key":"hPd2T7c5JM"}],"key":"ZcwYa9Cnm5"}],"identifier":"6fa10400","html_id":"6fa10400","key":"hIXxXal1Q3"}],"key":"eKMS8lNJst"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"CROCODILE 2026 Workshop Projects","short_title":"Projects","url":"/crocodash/projects","group":"Use Cases"},"next":{"title":"Project: CICE Configuration - Ayy, It’s Chilly!","url":"/crocodash/projects/cice","group":"Use Cases"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}